This code uses the Linux SPI driver to communicate with the MCP3008. It sets up the SPI device, opens the CSV file, and then enters a loop where it reads the voltage from each of the MCP3008's channels, writes the timestamp, channel number, and measured voltage to the CSV file, and then sleeps for 500 ms. If it encounters an error while reading or writing, it will retry up to 3 times before aborting. The program responds to a SIGINT by closing the SPI device and CSV file.

