This code uses the libgpiod library to interact with the GPIO lines of the Raspberry Pi. It first opens the GPIO chip, then gets the lines for the two sensors. It then requests these lines as input, and enters a loop where it reads the lines 5 times with a 2 ms delay between reads. It uses the majority value to avoid noise on the sensor signals. It prints the state of each sensor to the console, and if both sensors report an object, it prints an alert message. It also checks the return status of every API call and exits with an error message on failure. It installs a SIGINT handler that releases all GPIO resources on termination.

