This code assumes that the VL53L4CX sensor is connected to the Raspberry Pi Zero W on I2C bus 1, and that the address of the sensor is 0x29. It also assumes that the interrupt status register of the sensor is at address 0x18, and that a read operation on this register returns the distance measured by the sensor in mm. The code also assumes that the interrupt clear register of the sensor is at address 0x0B.

The code opens the I2C device, sets the address of the VL53L4CX sensor, and then enters an infinite loop where it reads the interrupt status register of the sensor every 500 ms. If the interrupt status bit is set, it clears the interrupt and logs the current timestamp and the measured distance to the console. The code also installs signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM to ensure that the I2C file descriptor is closed and the program exits cleanly when these signals are received.

