This code uses the standard Linux I2C device driver to communicate with the SDP810 sensor. It sends the measurement command, waits for the conversion time, reads the measurement data, validates the CRCs, and logs the pressure and temperature values. It gracefully handles interrupt signals and ensures that resources are released on exit.

Please note that you need to implement the `crc8` function and the `crc8.h` header file, which are not included in this code. The `crc8` function should implement the CRC-8 checksum algorithm as specified by the SDP810 sensor.

