Also, the `gpiod_line_close()` function is used to close the I2C line handle. If the I2C read fails, the code will attempt to close and reopen the I2C line handle before continuing. If the retry limit is exceeded, the program will exit.

The code installs signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM that will close the I2C line handle, flush and close the CSV file, and then exit the program.

