This code initializes the GPIO lines for the two sensors, sets up a signal handler for SIGINT and SIGTERM, and opens the log file. It then enters an infinite loop where it sleeps for one second at a time. The interrupt service routine (ISR) is triggered whenever the state of the GPIO lines changes, and it updates the log file with a timestamp and the direction of rotation based on the state of the lines. The code also checks for errors at each step and releases resources on exit.

