This code opens the GPIO chip, gets the line corresponding to the sensor, requests falling edge events, and opens the output file. It then enters an infinite loop where it waits for an event from the sensor. If an event is received, it gets the current time, formats it as a string, prints the string to stdout, and appends the string to the output file. When the program is interrupted or terminated, it releases the line, closes the chip, and closes the file before exiting.

