This code uses the libgpiod library to interact with the GPIO lines of the Raspberry Pi. It sets up a GPIO line for the sensor and another for the LED. It also opens a file for logging touch events. The main loop waits for a rising edge event on the sensor line. When it detects one, it checks if a debounce time has passed since the last touch. If it has, it logs the event and toggles the LED. The signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM call the cleanup functions and exit the program.

