This code first opens the GPIO chip, gets the line, requests falling edge events, and opens the log file. It then enters a loop where it waits for falling edge events. If an event is detected, it gets the current time, formats it as a string, and prints and logs the message. The code gracefully handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals by closing the GPIO line, the chip, and the log file before exiting. It also checks for errors on every driver library call and file operation, setting the exit status to `EXIT_FAILURE` if any error occurs.

