This code assumes that the I2C device file for the I2C bus that the BH1750 sensor is connected to is "/dev/i2c-1" and that the PWM device file for the PWM chip and line that the WS2812B strip is connected to is "/dev/pwm/pwmchip0/pwm0". You may need to adjust these paths depending on your hardware setup.

Also, note that this code uses the POSIX write and read system calls instead of the C library fwrite and fread functions, because the write and read system calls return the number of bytes written or read, which makes it easier to check for errors.

Finally, the code uses the POSIX usleep function to sleep for 180 ms after issuing the sensor command, because it is more portable than the C library sleep function.

