This code is a simple implementation of the requirements. It uses the standard POSIX and Linux kernel headers, and no external libraries. It reads the ambient light from a BH1750 digital light sensor on the I2C bus, stores the last 60 lux readings in a circular buffer, computes the average lux of the buffer, and blinks an LED connected to GPIO17 with a 50% duty cycle square wave whose frequency varies proportionally from 0.5 Hz in darkness to 5 Hz at bright levels (1000 + lux). If a sensor read fails, the program prints an error, skips that sample, and attempts a new read on the next loop iteration. On program termination via Ctrl+C, it catches SIGINT, cleansly releases the GPIO (unexports) and closes the I2C file descriptor.

