This code assumes that the accelerometer and magnetometer are correctly connected to the I2C bus 1 of the Raspberry Pi Zero W and that the I2C address of the device is 0x1E. The code also assumes that the actual computation of the heading depends on the accelerometer and magnetometer data, which is not provided here.

Please replace the placeholder for heading computation with the actual computation.

The code handles the signals SIGINT and SIGTERM to perform a graceful shutdown by closing the I2C file and the log file.

The code checks the result of every I2C operation and handles cases where the sensor is absent or the bus reports an error by exiting gracefully.

The code logs each sample with a timestamp, the computed heading, the three-axis acceleration in g, and the three-axis magnetic field in gauss to a file named compass_log.txt. The file is created if it does not exist and is truncated to zero length if it already exists. The code adds a CSV header when the file is created.

