This code uses the libgpiod library to monitor a GPIO line on a Raspberry Pi. It accepts a single command-line argument that is the threshold for the number of high readings in a window. The program will exit with an error if the argument is not a positive integer.

The program will handle SIGINT and SIGTERM signals by releasing the GPIO line and closing the GPIO chip before exiting.

The program will continuously monitor the GPIO line, printing a timestamped line to stdout for each window. The line will be "ALERT" if the count of high readings exceeds the threshold, otherwise it will be "OK". The program will then sleep for 1 second before starting the next window.

