This code assumes that the LSM303DLHC magnetometer is connected to the Raspberry Pi Zero W and that it provides X, Y, and Z magnetic field measurements that can be read directly from the device. The code also assumes that the sensor's 7-bit I2C address is 0x1E. The code uses the Linux I2C API to read from the I2C device. The code applies the hard-iron calibration offsets and computes a heading in degrees using the atan2 function. The code maps the heading to one of the eight compass directions and prints it to the console. The code logs each sample to a CSV file and checks the result of every open, ioctl, read, write, and fopen call. If the code encounters an I2C read failure, it writes a diagnostic message to stderr and skips that sample. The code installs a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler that cleanly closes the I2C file descriptor and the CSV file and frees all resources on every exit path.

