This code uses the libgpiod library to interact with the GPIO lines of the Raspberry Pi. It sets up a handler for SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to ensure a clean exit. The main loop waits for a rising edge event on the PIR sensor line, turns on the floodlight, logs the activation event, waits for 60 seconds, turns off the floodlight, logs the deactivation event, and repeats. If any system call or library function fails, it turns off the floodlight, closes the log file, releases the libgpiod resources, and exits with an error code.

