This code assumes that the Honeywell AWM7300V sensor is connected to the Raspberry Pi Zero W at I2C address 0x30. It uses the standard I2C system calls to communicate with the sensor, and a SIGINT handler to cleanly close the I2C file descriptor and log file when the program is interrupted. The sensor documentation is assumed to mask the 14‑bit airflow value with an AND operation using the hexadecimal value 0x3FFF. The code logs a timestamp and airflow value entry to a file named airflow_log.txt every second.

